WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:09.100
. As if Donald Trump needed any more scandals,
this could be the scandal of all scandals.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:17.510
We have learned that the Justice Department
is investigating a possible cash for Trump

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.030
pardons scheme.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:21.030
Understand what this means.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:25.640
The idea is there are people out there who
want to be pardoned by Donald Trump before

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.410
Trump leaves office in about seven weeks.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:36.199
The idea that is being investigated is that
you could pay someone to go and talk to Trump

00:00:36.199 --> 00:00:37.760
about pardoning you.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.539
And it is absolutely and utterly insane.

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:44.499
We knew Trump would issue corrupt and erroneous
pardons.

00:00:44.499 --> 00:00:45.499
He did so with Michael.

00:00:45.499 --> 00:00:52.729
And last week, he did so with Roger Stone
some months ago, but a cash for pardons scandal

00:00:52.729 --> 00:00:54.640
is another level altogether.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.670
And we learned about the existence of this
investigation because of the release of some

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:05.660
very redacted court documents that called
this a bribery for pardons scheme.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:10.500
A ton of the 18 page document that was released,
a ton of it is blacked out.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:11.760
It's redacted.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:16.850
Entire swaths, large sections, even almost
whole pages blacked out.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:22.140
Nobody who is involved has yet been named
in the redacted documents.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.950
Presumably they are named in the unredacted
documents.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:30.280
But what the document does say is that federal
prosecutors in Washington say they've obtained

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:37.579
evidence of a bribery scheme in which someone
would offer a big political contribution in

00:01:37.579 --> 00:01:42.799
exchange for a presidential pardon or reprieve
of sentence.

00:01:42.799 --> 00:01:44.369
The order said.

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:49.869
Prosecutors were also investigating a secret
lobbying scheme in which two unidentified

00:01:49.869 --> 00:01:58.259
individuals would lobby senior White House
officials about pardons without disclosing

00:01:58.259 --> 00:02:00.140
that, without being registered properly.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:04.869
As part of the Lobbying Disclosure Act, the
Justice Department wanted to keep this private

00:02:04.869 --> 00:02:10.260
because it detailed individuals and conduct
that hasn't yet led to charges.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:13.830
And it is an absolutely insane series of allegations.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:16.330
Now, I want to be really clear.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:20.650
Just because the pardons would ultimately
be issued by Donald Trump doesn't mean that

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:23.080
this was people giving Trump money for pardons.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.210
It's really important that we understand that.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:30.360
It wouldn't be surprising to me, given Trump's
massive debts, if people were offering Trump

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.080
money for pardons.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.220
That's not what we as of now believe is going
on.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:42.360
The idea for now seems to be that if you want
a pardon, you pay someone that someone goes

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:48.430
and talks to senior White House officials,
the idea being the White House officials then

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:54.650
go to Trump and maybe never disclose that
there is this whole bribery situation going

00:02:54.650 --> 00:03:00.410
on and say, hey, sir, Mr. President, you should
really look at pardoning this person or that

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.410
person.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:10.090
So it's still very early, but my mind goes
to how bad must this be if Donald Trump's

00:03:10.090 --> 00:03:15.090
own attorney general, William Barr's DOJ,
is investigating?

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:19.590
And what I mean by that is William Barr is
one of the most corrupt attorneys general

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:25.860
we've ever seen in terms of political cronyism
and partizanship even William Barr had to

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:30.940
say there's no evidence of widespread voter
fraud, which we covered earlier today.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:35.930
I can't imagine that William Barr would be
eager to bring charges for criminal pardon

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.220
bribery.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:41.980
But for William Barr to even have his Justice
Department investigating this means that there

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:46.380
has been a relatively high threshold met already.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:49.670
This entire issue of pardons, of course, is
a bigger issue.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:55.270
You know, imagine a president ordering people
to assassinate a political enemy and then

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:58.240
pardoning them as an example.

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:04.930
The entire pardon process and infrastructure
is riddled with corruption, cronyism, and

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:08.080
lends itself to all sorts of all sorts of
malfeasance.

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:14.050
But we are now getting to investigations that
are the types of things you see more often

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:19.040
in developing and poorer countries, not typically
the United States, but it's at least possibly

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:23.290
happening here, scandal after scandal after
scandal.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:27.210
And, you know, we've got seven weeks left.

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:33.370
What will we learn about in these last seven
weeks, what will Trump do in these last seven

00:04:33.370 --> 00:04:34.470
weeks?

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:38.060
And then once he's out of office, what are
we going to learn?

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:44.600
I don't believe that we will ever see Trump
indicted, prosecuted or jailed, as many of

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:48.870
my viewers would like to see and as some of
my viewers believe will happen.

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:53.261
But I do believe that there is going to be
another shoe that drops after Donald Trump

00:04:53.261 --> 00:04:59.520
is out of office about all sorts of allegations
of things he and the people around him did.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:04.540
And a lot of this explains why Donald Trump
is now considering pardoning preemptively

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.920
his own children, son in law and Rudy Giuliani.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.130
We will talk about that after the break.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:15.380
In the meantime, make sure you're following
me on Instagram at David Pakman.

